@startuml

title A derived market object: the states of a set

[*] --> Candidate : compute
Candidate --> Candidate : compute with changed\ninputs (a new version)
Candidate --> Raised : raise a publish\n(names the version;\nno blocking check failed)
Raised --> Published : a stated rule closes it\n(applied in the raise's\ntransaction)
Raised --> Approved : a person approves
Raised --> Closed : refused, withdrawn\nor expired
Approved --> Published : the trader applies\nwithin the apply window
Approved --> Closed : the apply window passes,\nor the apply is refused
Published --> Superseded : a set at the same or a\nnewer as-of is applied
Published --> Withdrawn : a withdrawal is\napproved and applied
Superseded --> Withdrawn : a withdrawal is\napproved and applied
Superseded --> [*]
Withdrawn --> [*]
Closed --> [*]

Candidate : stored, versioned, traceable
Candidate : not consumable
Raised : one open request\nper subject and as-of
Published : read by as-of under\nthe read rule
Superseded : still read for an as-of\nbefore its successor's,\nand after its successor\nis withdrawn
Withdrawn : no read by as-of takes it;\na binding still names it
Closed : nothing was published

@enduml
